# Task Execution

This rule intentionally stays thin to avoid overlap with the project skill:
`<runtime>/skills/task-execution/SKILL.md` (`.cursor` or `.claude`).

When a user asks to execute work from `PLANNING.md` (or update planning progress),
always apply that skill and follow its workflow.

Minimum enforcement:
- Keep `PLANNING.md` checklist status accurate (`[x]` for completed, `[ ]` otherwise).
- Ensure `## ✅ Done` reflects completed outcomes.
- Create/update `DECISIONS.md` with timestamp, what changed, and practical why.
- Create/update `RUN_LOG.md` with one execution row per batch.
- Enforce `RUN_LOG.md` retention: keep latest 30 entries only.

Execution is not complete until all checklist outcomes above are satisfied in files.

Do not duplicate detailed process here; maintain details in the skill only.
